/**

@page tarch_accelerator_SYCL SYCL support

\tableofcontents

Peano's technical architecture can be configured with SYCL support for GPU
offloading and, on some systems, for task execution. The concrete compiler flags
are vendor-specific, so the main setup instructions live on
@ref page_compiler_specific_settings_home "the compiler-specific settings page".

In practice, a SYCL build has to be configured with the corresponding GPU or
multithreading backend and compiled with a SYCL-capable C++ compiler. Intel
oneAPI, Codeplay-enabled Intel LLVM builds, and AdaptiveCpp-style toolchains all
need slightly different `CXXFLAGS` and `LDFLAGS`.

Use this page as the tarch-level entry point and the vendor page for exact
commands.

*/
